.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PKG-BE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg-be
.Nd create a ZFS boot environment before pkg operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm pkg be
.Cm list
.Op Fl av
.Nm pkg be
.Cm show
.Ar be
.Nm pkg be
.Cm diff
.Ar be
.Op Ar be2
.Nm pkg be
.Cm rollback
.Op Fl ty
.Ar be
.Nm pkg be
.Cm prune
.Op Fl n
.Pp
Enable the plugin in
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PKG_ENABLE_PLUGINS = true;
PLUGINS = [ "pkg-be" ];
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a
.Xr pkg 8
plugin.
Before
.Nm pkg
applies an upgrade (and, optionally, an install, delete or autoremove),
it creates a boot environment with
.Xr libbe 3 .
If the change breaks the system, the previous state can be booted with
.Xr bectl 8 .
.Pp
The boot environment is named
.Sm off
.Ar PREFIX No - Ar YYYYmmdd No - Ar HHMMSS ,
.Sm on
with a
.Sm off
.No - Ar N
.Sm on
suffix if that name already exists.
.Pp
After creating it,
.Nm
destroys the oldest boot environments whose names match
.Ar PREFIX
so that at most
.Va BE_KEEP
of them remain.
Boot environments with other names are never touched.
The active and the next-boot environments are never destroyed.
.Pp
Nothing is done when
.Nm pkg
runs with
.Fl n
(dry run), with
.Fl r Ar rootdir
(another system is changed), with
.Fl c Ar chroot ,
inside a jail
.Pq including Nm pkg Fl j ,
or when the root file system is not on ZFS boot environments.
.Pp
The newest boot environment of
.Nm
is never destroyed by the retention rules.
.Sh COMMANDS
The plugin adds a
.Cm be
subcommand to
.Xr pkg 8 .
.Bl -tag -width rollback
.It Cm list Op Fl av
List boot environments created by
.Nm
with their creation time, operation, number of changes and the
changes themselves.
The ACTIVE column uses the
.Xr bectl 8
flags: N is active now, R is active on reboot.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
List all boot environments, not only those of
.Nm .
.It Fl v
Do not shorten the CHANGES column.
.El
.It Cm show Ar be
Show the details of one boot environment, one change per line.
.It Cm diff Ar be Op Ar be2
Compare the installed packages of
.Ar be
with those of the running system, or with those of
.Ar be2 .
Boot environments other than the running one are mounted temporarily.
Requires root.
.It Cm rollback Oo Fl ty Oc Ar be
Activate
.Ar be
so that it is booted on the next reboot.
Requires root.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t
Activate for the next boot only.
.It Fl y
Do not ask for confirmation.
.El
.It Cm prune Op Fl n
Apply the
.Va BE_KEEP ,
.Va BE_KEEP_AGE
and
.Va BE_MIN_AGE
retention now.
With
.Fl n ,
only print what would be destroyed.
Requires root unless
.Fl n
is given.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.Pa pkg-be.conf
in the
.Va PLUGINS_CONF_DIR
directory of
.Xr pkg.conf 5 :
.Bl -tag -width BE_ENABLED
.It Va BE_ENABLED
Boolean.
Default
.Dq true .
.It Va BE_PREFIX
Name prefix.
Default
.Dq pkg-be .
.It Va BE_KEEP
Number of boot environments to keep.
0 keeps all.
Default 5.
.It Va BE_KEEP_AGE
Also destroy boot environments older than this duration, judged by the
time in their name.
A duration is a number with an optional suffix
.Cm s ,
.Cm m ,
.Cm h ,
.Cm d
or
.Cm w ,
for example
.Dq 30d ;
without a suffix it is seconds.
At most 2^31-1 seconds.
0 disables this rule.
Default
.Dq 0 .
The newest boot environment is never destroyed.
.It Va BE_KEEP_DAYS
Older form of
.Va BE_KEEP_AGE
in whole days.
Ignored when
.Va BE_KEEP_AGE
is not 0.
.It Va BE_MIN_AGE
Never destroy boot environments younger than this duration, even if
.Va BE_KEEP
or
.Va BE_KEEP_AGE
would.
More than
.Va BE_KEEP
may then remain.
0 disables this rule.
Default
.Dq 0 .
.Pp
If a duration is invalid, boot environments are still created but none
are destroyed, and an error is shown.
.It Va BE_REPOSITORIES
Create a boot environment only if at least one package of the operation
comes from one of these repositories (comma or space separated, case
sensitive).
The word
.Cm local
means packages that do not come from a repository, such as those
installed with
.Cm pkg add .
Empty means any repository.
Default empty.
.It Va BE_MIN_FREE
Warn when the pool has less than this percentage of free space.
0 disables the warning.
Default 10.
.It Va BE_SYSLOG
Boolean.
Also log creation, destruction and errors with
.Xr syslog 3
(facility user, ident of
.Xr pkg 8 ,
text starting with
.Dq pkg-be: ) .
.Va SYSLOG No = false in
.Xr pkg.conf 5
also turns this off.
Default
.Dq true .
.It Va BE_HOOKS
Comma or space separated list of operations that create a boot
environment:
.Cm upgrade ,
.Cm install ,
.Cm deinstall
.Pq or Cm delete ,
.Cm autoremove ,
.Cm all
or
.Cm none .
Default
.Dq upgrade .
.El
.Sh PROPERTIES
Each boot environment gets these ZFS user properties:
.Bl -tag -width pkg-be:packages
.It Va pkg-be:op
Operation that triggered it, for example
.Dq upgrade .
.It Va pkg-be:packages
Planned changes:
.Dq +name-ver
(install),
.Dq -name-ver
(delete),
.Dq name old->new
(upgrade).
Long lists end with
.Dq ... (+N more) .
.It Va pkg-be:count
Number of planned changes.
.It Va pkg-be:version
.Nm
version.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/pkg/pkg-be.conf" -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/lib/pkg/pkg-be.so
the plugin
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/pkg-be.conf
configuration
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm pkg be
exits 0 on success and >0 on error, using the values from
.Xr sysexits 3 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a boot environment before upgrades and installs, keep ten:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
BE_HOOKS = "upgrade, install";
BE_KEEP = 10;
.Ed
.Pp
Only for base system updates (pkgbase), keep a month, never destroy one
from the last day:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
BE_REPOSITORIES = "FreeBSD-base";
BE_KEEP_AGE = "30d";
BE_MIN_AGE = "1d";
.Ed
.Pp
Find the boot environment taken before a bad upgrade, check what has
changed since, and boot back into it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pkg be list
pkg be diff pkg-be-20261110-123807
pkg be rollback pkg-be-20261110-123807
shutdown -r now
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libbe 3 ,
.Xr sysexits 3 ,
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr pkg.conf 5 ,
.Xr bectl 8 ,
.Xr pkg 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Mehmet Ozgan Aq Mt mozgan@gmail.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Xr pkg 8
ignores the plugin return value: if the boot environment cannot be
created, the operation still proceeds.
Plugins are disabled in
.Nm pkg-static .
With
.Fl r Ar rootdir ,
.Nm pkg
loads plugins and
.Pa pkg.conf
from
.Ar rootdir ;
.Nm
only skips if it is installed and enabled there.
Data on datasets outside the boot environment, such as
.Pa /home ,
is not part of the boot environment and is not rolled back.
